# Per-repo allowlist for the global secret-guard (~/.git-hooks/pre-commit).
# Reviewed 2026-11-18: every entry below is a deliberate SHIPMENT, not a
# secret. Patterns are case-insensitive regexes matched against staged
# filenames AND added lines; # comments are ignored.
#
# Keep patterns TIGHT: an over-broad allow (e.g. bare "PRIVATE KEY") would
# exempt a real leak in some future file. Each pattern names the exact shape
# it forgives.

# 1) The secret scanner and its self-test ship by design. Their filenames
#    contain "secrets." (the guard's path token aimed at secrets.json-style
#    files), and their SOURCE must contain detection patterns and fake
#    samples in order to be tested — a scanner without them proves nothing.
scripts/scan_secrets\.py
tests/test_scan_secrets\.py

# 2) blnq-cli.py lines that READ credentials from env/state — variable
#    names and .get() calls, never literals.
token = _get_or_create_auth_token
auth_token = _get_or_create_auth_token
environ\.get\("BLNQ_TOKEN"\)

# 3) Fake fixtures inside the scanner self-test: the throwaway test token
#    (only in its documented usage line), the synthetic key blocks whose
#    bodies are the literal {BLOB} placeholder, and the pg-tooling env READ.
admintest123
PRIVATE KEY-----\\n\{BLOB\}
PGPASSWORD=os\.environ\.get
